WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.000
The result: Beacon, a working local uptime monitor. Real HTTP fixture results.

00:06.000 --> 00:14.000
In Abralo, the operator gives the backend engineer a detailed build brief.

00:14.000 --> 00:20.000
The backend engineer builds the service and hands the API contract to the interface engineer.

00:20.000 --> 00:26.000
The interface engineer implements the dashboard, then hands it to the reviewer. Waiting omitted.

00:26.000 --> 00:34.000
The reviewer finds a content-type validation defect. The operator requests a narrow fix.

00:34.000 --> 00:42.000
The backend engineer fixes it. All 17 unchanged regression tests pass.

00:42.000 --> 00:48.000
The operator accepts a local prototype. Docker remains untested; no production approval.

00:48.000 --> 00:56.000
The generated dashboard tracks an actual local fixture's outage and recovery. Inspect the source below.
